# T_SCRR: a user edited from the list: OPER disabled (its row marked),
# renamed, regrouped and made level 3; then given a new password typed
# twice, first one too short, which the server refuses (its text shown
# on the password), then one it takes, with a new full name (USER
# RESET, then USER SET, checked by T_SCRR; the user must change the
# password at the next login); READER deleted after the question; and
# the last active administrator refused a lower level by the server.  F1
# shows the help of the form.  Ctrl-F, a global key, leaves the list for the
# search, which this test does not run; at the home screen F1 then shows
# nothing, the users' help topic being put back.  Then the user's own
# password is changed (SCMD_PASSWD).
S USERS
